<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer stock sale earlier on Friday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN     TONNES   PORT	 QUALITY     U.S. DLR/T</p>
<p> Cameroon     100    Amsterdam    FF	    1,265</p>
<p> Cameroon     180    Amsterdam    GF	    1,250</p>
<p> Ivory Coast   10    Amsterdam    FF	    1,270</p>
<p> Ivory Coast  149    Amsterdam    FF	    1,280</p>
<p> Ivory Coast  322    Amsterdam    GF	  1,335 - 1,355</p>
<p> Ghana	  254    Amsterdam    GF	    1,395</p>
<p> Ghana	  397    Hull	   GF	  1,424 - 1,452</p>
<p> Ghana	  298    Hull	   FF	  1,410 - 1,419</p>
<p> Ghana	1,290    Hull	   GF	  1,427 - 1,452</p>
<p> Nigeria	139    Amsterdam    FF	    1,280</p>
<p> Nigeria	 99    Amsterdam    GF	    1,280</p>
<p> Nigeria	249    Amsterdam    FF	    1,280</p>
<p> Nigeria	249    Amsterdam    GF	    1,351</p>
<p> Ivory Coast  148    Amsterdam    FAQ	 1,240 - 1,270</p>
<p> Ivory Coast   51    Amsterdam    FAQ	   1,295</p>
<p> Nigeria	315    Amsterdam    FAQ	   1,240</p>
<p>(GF = good fermented, FF = fair fermented)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
